  defects: [
    { n: 1, cls: "framework", rung: 6, t: "Reset did nothing", d: "React overrides the name of a button whose form action is a function, so the setting’s key never arrived.", fix: "Bind the key to the action." },
    { n: 2, cls: "framework", rung: 6, t: "Headings never saved", d: "The editor keeps attributes in objects without a prototype, which a Server Action cannot receive. It also broke headings in reports.", fix: "The editor sends plain JSON." },
    { n: 3, cls: "cascade", rung: 8, t: "The quick exit covered the header", d: "The bevel class sets position: relative, which beat position: fixed.", fix: "A positioned wrapper." },
    { n: 4, cls: "language", rung: 6, t: "‘petrol’ was redacted", d: "The stem of ‘Peter’, the giver, matched ‘petrol’ in ‘3 kW petrol generator’.", fix: "Stems of at least four letters and endings of at most four; a regression test." },
    { n: 5, cls: "semantics", rung: 6, t: "Every setting became ‘custom’", d: "Saving one group recorded every value in it, so the labels that say where a value comes from were wrong.", fix: "Unchanged values are not recorded; a test." },
    { n: 6, cls: "cascade", rung: 8, t: "A name squeezed to ‘Те…’", d: "In Ukrainian, the navigation squeezed the organisation’s name to two letters at 1440 pixels.", fix: "A two-row header on every screen." },
    { n: 7, cls: "params", rung: 6, t: "Section numbers out of order", d: "Numbers were fixed per component, so after reordering the home page read § 02, § 01…", fix: "Numbers follow the rendered order." },
    { n: 8, cls: "scenario", rung: 6, t: "A gift never reached ‘Thanked’", d: "The status existed, but no event ever set it.", fix: "gift.Acknowledged when thanks are shared." },
    { n: 9, cls: "scenario", rung: 6, t: "The walk could not be completed", d: "The carrier had no delivery on the way, and the recipient had nothing to confirm.", fix: "A second request and a delivery in the seed; a test that the demo is walkable." },
    { n: 10, cls: "params", rung: 8, t: "A 73% cost share", d: "The state programme showed 73% of its money going on delivery, an artefact of scaling pounds into hryvnias.", fix: "Credible amounts for that profile." },
    { n: 11, cls: "cascade", rung: 8, t: "Seven stages overflowed", d: "The administrator’s studio stages overflowed at 1440 pixels.", fix: "Equal columns without icons." },
    { n: 12, cls: "framework", rung: 6, t: "The studio’s tab said ‘home’", d: "Studio pages carried the home page’s title in the browser tab.", fix: "A studio title." },
    { n: 13, cls: "language", rung: 6, t: "‘Every pound’ in a hryvnia fund", d: "‘Every pound’, ‘£1 to £100,000’ and ‘£250’ in the texts were wrong for the profiles that count in hryvnias.", fix: "Neutral wording, or values from settings." },
  ],

  /* Sheet 06: layers of understanding, oldest first. */
  strata: [
    { m: "M1", title: "A gift is not a commodity", understood: "The portal must not sell good deeds. There is no basket of donations and no ranking of people in need; help is matched to the shape of a need: what, where, when and in what form.", missed: "How much of this is about dignity rather than efficiency. I learnt that later, from the words the pages use: ‘Share what you can’, ‘Your request’.", went: "Matching (DP-04), the tone of voice, the give page." },
    { m: "M1", title: "The river remembers", understood: "Trust needs a record that cannot be rewritten: an append-only log, with every page a projection of it.", missed: "That the same idea would later shape the process itself: the reflections are versioned, never edited.", went: "@river/log, page documents, ADR-0011 and ADR-0012." },
    { m: "M1–M2", title: "Privacy first, in a conflict zone", understood: "A person asking for help may be in danger if identified. Personal details never enter the log; public stories wait at least 14 days and name only the oblast.", missed: "That redaction must understand grammar: in Ukrainian, a village’s name changes its ending.", went: "Private documents, redaction, the 14-day floor, pseudonymised reports." },
    { m: "M2", title: "An open question is not a stop sign", understood: "Take the nearest variant, write it down, and keep going. Unknowns are recorded, not waited for.", missed: "Nothing, at the time. The cost came later: some nearest variants were never revisited.", went: "Open questions, working agreements, decision records written as built." },
    { m: "M3", title: "Openness has a look", understood: "A drafting table says ‘the plan is open’. Numbers set as dimensions feel measured rather than promotional, and warmth belongs where people speak.", missed: "How far a visual language carries: it reached the studio, the card and this almanac.", went: "ADR-0018, the whole interface, this almanac’s own sheets." },
    { m: "M4", title: "Why it exists", understood: "The portal is a free template and a way to draw attention to Oleshky, a town in Kherson oblast, occupied and under blockade. The openness of the left bank is not a feature; it is the reason.", missed: "I noticed only later that Oleshky itself stands on the left bank of the Dnipro.", went: "The disclaimer, the licences, the dedication on sheet 08." },
    { m: "M5", title: "Seeing the whole river", understood: "The model could not be walked: no identities for the roles, no trust for a first visitor, no emergency route for a person in danger.", missed: "That my own review would be the thing that changed direction, rather than more building.", went: "Vectors V1 to V8; iteration 04." },
    { m: "M6", title: "Many organisations, one river", understood: "A charity is not one thing. A state programme, a city foundation and a small group abroad need different currencies, limits and words, and some rules must never loosen.", missed: "That ‘correct’ would become plural: a text that is right for one profile can be wrong for another.", went: "The settings registry, three profiles, floors, the screenshot matrix." },
    { m: "M7–M10", title: "The process mirrors the product", understood: "The way we worked had the same shape as the portal: an append-only record, projections, parameters with floors, roles acting in a capacity, and never blocking on an open question. The scarce resource is the steward’s attention.", missed: "Whether a reader who was not there can follow it. This almanac is the test.", went: "The reflection vault, the card, this almanac." },
  ],

